# Studio Product Framework

- Monorepo is agent-native: prefer changes that keep web + packages + agents coherent.
- Apps orchestrate (auth, policy, status). Packages expose composable capability blocks with explicit inputs + structured results. No god services. No package DB writes.
- Client never touches the database — Convex only.
- Effect (`@studio/effect-critical`) only for money, inference, delivery.
- Runtime agents require sandboxes (`@studio/ai-runtime`). Builder agents use `agents/`.
- Billing: Polar + Stripe (subscriptions) and Autumn (credits) are all first-class.
- Observability: PostHog for product analytics/flags; Sentry for errors.
- Shared agent memory: Hivemind (Deeplake) — capture on by default via `.hivemind`; git (`agents/`, `docs/`) remains durable truth. See `docs/hivemind.md`.
- Before merging UI: Rams skill / Rams GitHub App. Before merging code: Greptile + greploop.
- Framework improvement: `research` → queue → `improve-framework` (depth ≤3, no auto-merge). Handover via `operate-handover` — operators own tweaks after 1–2 Studio iterations.
- Venture products: `score-problem` → `commit-v1` (discovery artifacts under `agents/context/discovery/`) before bootstrap. Platform plumbing may skip.
- Public Convex functions: auth, args+returns validators, await promises, indexes over filter, paginate unbounded lists.
- Prefer `docs/capabilities.md`, `docs/loop-engineering.md`, and `agents/AGENTS.md` over inventing new structure.
